\section*{A spherical distribution of the low-temperature total quantum spin}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
OpenAI presents a proof in the selected manuscript. At low fixed temperature, symmetric zero-field magnetization is claimed to approach a uniformly oriented vector of deterministic positive magnitude equal to the right pressure derivative.

\subsection{Mathematical statement of the claimed result}
\paragraph{Result 1.} On the even-side torus \(\Lambda_L=(\mathbb Z/L\mathbb Z)^3\), set \(V=L^3\), \(H_{S,L}=-\sum_{\{x,y\}\text{ nearest neighbors}}\boldsymbol S_x\cdot\boldsymbol S_y\), and \(M_L^a=\sum_xS_x^a\). For each fixed $S\in\{1/2,1,3/2,\ldots\}$, the claim provides finite \(\beta_0(S)\) so that any finite \(\beta\ge\beta_0\) has positive spontaneous magnetization \(m=p'_{S,\beta}(0+)\). With zero-field Gibbs expectation,
\[
 \lim_{L\to\infty,\ L\text{ even}}
 \left\langle\exp\!\left(V^{-1}\sum_{a=1}^3t_aM_L^a\right)\right\rangle_{\beta,L}
 =\frac1{4\pi}\int_{S^2}e^{m t\cdot n}\,d\sigma(n)
 =\frac{\sinh(m|t|)}{m|t|}\qquad(t\in\mathbb R^3).
\]
The value at \(t=0\) is one. The same limit gives \(V^{-2}\sum_{x,y}\langle\boldsymbol S_x\cdot\boldsymbol S_y\rangle\to m^2\).

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
Exchange-cycle pins and zero-free traces control torus comparisons at vanishing field. Removing the field across spatial scales and suppressing replica cross terms identifies the moment law; pressure tangents determine its radius without assigning joint measurements to noncommuting components.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
At low fixed temperature, symmetric zero-field magnetization is claimed to approach a uniformly oriented vector of deterministic positive magnitude equal to the right pressure derivative. The question retains these same parameters and conventions. Within these assumptions, this is a claimed affirmative answer to the stated question.

\subsection{Formal verification}
For family 271, the selected theorem constructs low-temperature zero-field magnetized KMS states for all dimensions at least three and all positive spins. The Bloch expansion, lattice correction, and spherical moment law are separate unselected companions. No Comparator is assigned to the selected manuscript here; the family page selects other papers or supporting statements. This site has not executed the Lean code. The scope descriptions do not certify the remaining manuscript arguments.

